From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:34:35 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] qwen3_5: mHC in its own image and module; the loop plan
 in its own

The forward, geometry and engine were at or past the 600-line cap and the mHC
kernels pushed qwen35.cu over it, so they move rather than grow:

- zig/kernels/cuda/qwen35_mhc.cu: the four mHC kernels, their own fatbin
  (catalog entry, kernels.zig blob, engine module 19), launched through the
  checked launch() so the host signature scanner still sees them.
- cuda_mhc.zig: the image's install and the four launches the forward makes.
- cuda_loop_plan.zig: loop_settings and mhc, read from the root config;
  cuda_loop_plan_test.zig pins this checkpoint's 56 executions, 14 attention and
  42 delta slots at SenseNova-Loop-9B's own shape.
- TF_Q35_DEBUG is a declared setting (platform/environment.zig), not a raw getenv.

zig fmt --check clean; lean_check 221 problems at base and head (zero new).
